Add a --by-owner flag to `velero backup item-outcomes`, rolling each item's outcome up to the object that owns it so a failed disk is reported against its virtual machine rather than a standalone row; the rollup consults the backup's volume info so a volume skipped in favour of another backup method is not reported as a failure. Table output indents the ownership chains so the rows behind a verdict stay visible, with --all showing every item rather than only the chains that failed or warned, and -o table|json|tree chooses the format, with tree rendering the forest as plain text
